creating directories, etc.</li>\n","\n","<li>imghdr: imghdr is a library used to determine the image type of a file or byte stream. It is used to ensure that the images being processed are of the correct type.</li>\n","\n","<li>pathlib: pathlib is a library used to interact with the file system. It is used to work with paths and file operations.</li>\n","\n","<li>random: random is a library used for generating pseudo-random numbers in Python. It is used to shuffle the dataset to improve model training.</li>\n","\n","<li>urllib: urllib is a library used for opening URLs. It is used to download the images from URLs.</li>\n","\n","<li>requests: requests is a library used to send HTTP requests using Python. It is used to download the images from URLs.</li>\n","\n","<li>BeautifulSoup: BeautifulSoup is a library used for web scraping purposes to pull the data out of HTML and XML files. It is used to extract the image URLs from web pages.</li>\n","\n","<li>mimetypes: mimetypes is a library used to map filenames to MIME types. It is used to ensure that the images being processed are of the correct type.\n","\n","<li>cv2: cv2 is an OpenCV library used for image processing purposes. It is used to preprocess the images for model training.\n","\n","<li>PIL: PIL is a Python Imaging Library used for opening, manipulating, and saving many different image file formats. It is used to preprocess the images for model training.\n","\n","<li>torch: torch is a PyTorch library used for building and training deep learning models. It is used for building and training the classification model.\n","\n","<li>torch.nn: torch.nn is a PyTorch module used for building neural networks. It is used for building the neural network architecture.\n","\n","<li>torch.optim: torch.optim is a PyTorch module used for optimizing the neural network. It is used for optimizing the neural network parameters.\n","\n","<li>DataLoader: DataLoader is a PyTorch class used for loading data in batches. It is used for loading the dataset for model training.\n","\n","<li>random_split: random_split is a PyTorch function used for splitting the dataset randomly. It is used for splitting the dataset into training and validation sets.\n","\n","<li>transforms: transforms is a PyTorch module used for image transformations. It is used for preprocessing the images for model training.\n","\n","<li>ImageFolder: ImageFolder is a PyTorch class used for loading image data from a directory. It is used for loading the dataset for model training.\n","\n","<li>models: models is a PyTorch module containing pre-trained models. It is used for loading a pre-trained model architecture.\n","\n","<li>ConfusionMatrix: ConfusionMatrix is a PyTorchMetrics class used for computing the confusion matrix for multiclass classification problems. It is used for evaluating the model performance.\n","\n","<li>sklearn: sklearn is a library containing a collection of machine learning algorithms and tools. It is used for evaluating the model performance."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"alL5xdWJVzs_"},"outputs":[],"source":["import numpy as np\n","import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n","import seaborn as sns\n","from tqdm.notebook import trange, tqdm\n","import os\n","import imghdr\n","import pathlib\n","from pathlib import Path\n","import random\n","import urllib\n","import requests\n","from bs4 import BeautifulSoup\n","import mimetypes\n","import cv2\n","from PIL import Image\n","\n","import torch as tc\n","import torch.nn as nn\n","import torch.optim as optim\n","from torch.utils.data import DataLoader\n","from torch.utils.data import random_split\n","from torchvision import transforms\n","from torchvision.datasets import ImageFolder\n","import torchvision.models as models\n","from torchmetrics import ConfusionMatrix\n","\n","import sklearn\n","from sklearn.metrics import accuracy_score, classification_report"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"VCcuzV4sF2ZZ"},"outputs":[],"source":["# Handle warnings\n","import warnings\n","warnings.filterwarnings(\"ignore\")"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"F5ekiKVWbJUm"},"source":["# Web Scrapping fruit images from Bing"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"T6KS1L10nta6"},"outputs":[],"source":["# Define the list of fruits and categories to scrape\n","fruits = ['apple', 'banana', 'mangoe', 'avocado', 'strawberry']\n","categories = ['unripe', 'ripe', 'rotten']"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"VmJUj82M04gD"},"source":["With the use of beautifulsoup library as stated in the objectives, we will be web scraping our fruit images for each class (unripe, ripe and rotten).\n","Our images will be scraped from Bing.com"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"IzUCKRS36T0r"},"outputs":[],"source":["# Snippet from (https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/image-scraping-with-python/)\n","# Loop over each fruit and category combination to scrape images\n","for fruit in fruits:\n","    for category in categories:\n","        # Define the URL of the search results page for the current fruit and category\n","        url = f'https://www.bing.com/images/search?q={category}+{fruit}'\n","        response = requests.get(url)\n","        soup = BeautifulSoup(response.content, 'html.parser')\n","        images = soup.find_all('img', class_='mimg')\n","\n","        save_dir = f'images/{category}_{fruit}/'\n","        if not os.path.exists(save_dir):\n","            os.makedirs(save_dir)\n","\n","        for i, image in enumerate(images):\n","            image_url = image.get('src') or image.get('data-src')\n","            # Define the filename for the image and download\n","            filename = f'{save_dir}{category}_{fruit}_{i}.jpg'\n","            urllib.request.urlretrieve(image_url, filename)"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"kIrJEfNS_oSL"},"source":["Let's check how many images we were able to scrape for each catergory and fruits. (i.e Each class)"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"NrSSi2z1dRJ_"},"outputs":[],"source":["# Create function to print the number of images in each class\n","def image_cnt_class(dir, classes):\n","  # Iterate through each class in classes list\n","  for class_name in classes:\n","    class_dir = os.path.join(dir, class_name)\n","    num_images = len([f for f in os.listdir(class_dir) if os.path.isfile(os.path.join(class_dir, f))])\n","    # Print the number of images for each class\n","    print(f'Number of images in class {class_name}: {num_images}')"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"1SfuIwV-DbN3"},"outputs":[],"source":["# Set the data directory path containing the images\n","data_dir = 'images'\n","# Create a list of the classes\n","classes = [f'{category}_{fruit}' for category in categories for fruit in fruits]"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"4ai92W7Q_Rm4","outputId":"cb5cad8c-9755-4498-ce07-10f05faec72f"},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["['unripe_apple', 'unripe_banana', 'unripe_mangoe', 'unripe_avocado', 'unripe_strawberry', 'ripe_apple', 'ripe_banana', 'ripe_mangoe', 'ripe_avocado', 'ripe_strawberry', 'rotten_apple', 'rotten_banana', 'rotten_mangoe', 'rotten_avocado', 'rotten_strawberry']\n"]}],"source":["# Print the classes\n","print(classes)"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"bHy4owzCDPN9","outputId":"e72f93a5-0317-4676-a740-805649e184f3"},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Number of images in class unripe_apple: 35\n","Number of images in class unripe_banana: 35\n","Number of images in class unripe_mangoe: 35\n","Number of images in class unripe_avocado: 35\n","Number of images in class unripe_strawberry: 35\n","Number of images in class ripe_apple: 35\n","Number of images in class ripe_banana: 35\n","