nd.jupyter.widget-view+json":{"model_id":"dcd3a2ff458d414091fab5235a398a80","version_major":2,"version_minor":0},"text/plain":["  0%|          | 0/53 [00:00<?, ?it/s]"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"},{"data":{"application/vnd.jupyter.widget-view+json":{"model_id":"f8104f477dbb4226b7ece410c150e0c6","version_major":2,"version_minor":0},"text/plain":["  0%|          | 0/7 [00:00<?, ?it/s]"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"},{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["epoch: 9\ttraining loss: 3.7979\tvalidation loss: 3.7537\tvalidation accuracy: 0.02\n","CPU times: user 18.5 s, sys: 2.3 s, total: 20.8 s\n","Wall time: 28.3 s\n"]},{"data":{"text/plain":["([6.7659783,\n","  6.3600807,\n","  5.9741373,\n","  5.592078,\n","  5.234033,\n","  4.883557,\n","  4.5592494,\n","  4.275039,\n","  4.0216146,\n","  3.797946],\n"," [6.7011447,\n","  6.22751,\n","  5.8214884,\n","  5.423886,\n","  5.0447946,\n","  4.8268447,\n","  4.4430366,\n","  4.1285615,\n","  3.9453294,\n","  3.7536902])"]},"execution_count":286,"metadata":{},"output_type":"execute_result"},{"data":{"image/png":"\n","text/plain":["<Figure size 1600x400 with 1 Axes>"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"}],"source":["%%time\n","fit(mbnet.cuda(), train_dl, val_dl, epochs=10, lr=1e-5);"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"ZuO4DoXYkisj"},"source":["# Transfer Learning\n","<p style=\"font-family:Georgia;\">A machine learning approach called transfer learning involves taking a model that has already been trained for one job and applying it to another that is somewhat similar.  The concept behind transfer learning is that a model that has already been trained may use a collection of characteristics that were learnt to do the original job to perform the new assignment, perhaps requiring less training data and less time.\n","<p style=\"font-family:Georgia;\">Transfer learning is the use of pre-trained convolutional neural network (CNN) models that were trained on sizable datasets like ImageNet in the context of deep learning and computer vision. These models are capable of creating high-level representations of pictures that may be utilised for a number of downstream tasks since they have learnt to recognise a wide range of elements in images, including as edges, forms, and textures.\n","<p style=\"font-family:Georgia;\"> Transfer learning may be done in a variety of methods, depending on the size of the new dataset and how similar the new job is to the original task. One typical method is to train a new classifier on top of the extracted features using the pre-trained CNN as a fixed feature extractor. Another method is to fine-tune the pre-trained CNN by retraining it using the new dataset with a slow learning rate. This method enables the model to adapt to the new job while preserving the pre-trained features.\n","<p style=\"font-family:Georgia;\"> For a variety of computer vision applications, including picture classification, object recognition, segmentation, and more, transfer learning has been proved to be a very successful method. It is especially helpful in situations when there is a lack of training data or the training procedure is computationally expensive since it may significantly reduce the quantity of training data and time needed to construct a high-performing model."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"Gg75-_oCnFHB"},"outputs":[],"source":["imagenet_stats = ([0.485, 0.456, 0.406], [0.229, 0.224, 0.225])\n","\n","transf_pt = transforms.Compose([\n","    transforms.Resize((224, 224)),    # Resized the images to (224 by 224) because it is the default input size for the pre-trained models\n","    transforms.ToTensor(),\n","    transforms.Normalize(*imagenet_stats)\n","])"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"cZmfPFqan5Qo"},"outputs":[],"source":["# Set the path to your image directory\n","image_dir = \"/content/images\""]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"7sJGse4Dn7zv"},"outputs":[],"source":["# Load the dataset applying the transform from above\n","dataset_pt = ImageFolder(root=image_dir, transform=transf_pt)"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"z_QMtC3qn13D"},"outputs":[],"source":["# Split the dataset into training and validation subsets\n","train_size = int(0.8 * len(dataset_pt))\n","val_size = len(dataset_pt) - train_size\n","train_ds_pt, val_ds_pt = random_split(dataset_pt, [train_size, val_size])"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"Xr5VgWeKng6A"},"outputs":[],"source":["batch_size = 8\n","# Create data loaders for training and validation subsets\n","train_dl_pt = DataLoader(train_ds_pt, batch_size=batch_size, shuffle=True, num_workers=2)\n","val_dl_pt = DataLoader(val_ds_pt, batch_size=2*batch_size, shuffle=False, num_workers=2)"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"ugXfXtFAm422"},"outputs":[],"source":["# Snippet from Lectures\n","def freeze(md, fr=True):\n","    ch = list(md.children())\n","    for c in ch: freeze(c, fr)\n","    if not ch and not isinstance(md, tc.nn.modules.batchnorm.BatchNorm2d):  # not freezing the BatchNorm layers!\n","        for p in md.parameters():\n","#             print('---\\n', md, p.requires_grad)\n","            p.requires_grad = not fr"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"54wTEw7Toy22"},"outputs":[],"source":["# Snippet from Lectures\n","def freeze_to(md, ix=-1, fr=True):\n","    ch_all = list(md.children())\n","    for ch in ch_all[:ix]:\n","        freeze(ch, fr)"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"WqkuIMfpzRGG"},"source":["## Fine-tuning ResNet18\n","<p style=\"font-family:Georgia;\"> Fine-tuning ResNet18 involves taking a pre-trained ResNet18 model that was trained on a large dataset such as ImageNet and adapting it to a new but related task. The basic idea is to reuse the learned features from the pre-trained model and fine-tune the model on a new dataset that has a different set of classes or labels.\n","\n","<ol style=\"font-family:Georgia;\">The steps involved in fine-tuning ResNet18 are as follows:\n","<li> Replace the final fully connected layer: The final layer of the pre-trained ResNet18 model is a fully connected layer with 1000 output neurons corresponding to the number of classes in ImageNet. This layer needs to be replaced with a new fully connected layer with the number of output neurons equal to the number of classes in the new dataset.\n","\n","<li>Freeze the pre-trained layers: The weights of the pre-trained layers are frozen so that only the weights of the new fully connected layer are updated during training. This ensures that the learned features from the pre-trained model are preserved and only the classification layer is adapted to the new task.\n","\n","<li>Train the model: The model is trained on the new dataset with a small learning rate, allowing the weights of the new fully connected layer to be updated gradually while preserving the learned features of the pre-trained layers.\n","\n","<li>Unfreeze some layers: If the performance of the fine-tuned model is not satisfactory, some of the pre-trained layers can be unfrozen and the model can be trained again with a lower learning rate. This allows the learned features from the pre-trained model to be further adapted to the new task.\n","\n","<p style=\"font-family:Georgia;\">Fine-tuning While using the learnt features from the pre-trained model, ResNet18 can drastically minimise the quantity of training data and time needed to construct a high-performing model for a new assignment. It is a potent method that has demonstrated success in a range of computer vision applications, including segmentation, object identification, and picture classification."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"rAw4cGdwkn-2"},"outputs":[],"source":["resnet18pre_train = models.resnet18(pretrained=True)\n","num_classes = 15\n","resnet18pre_train.fc = nn.Linear(512, num_classes)"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"zCkxY0c4zVA1"},"outputs":[],"source":["freeze_to(resnet18pre_train, -2, False)"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":577,"referenced_widgets":["cfeb5147a3c745b6be48b55212710c7c","3a1812d6e1b54c84a0c2c381f3fafa1c","1d23909433c64d7e8d9f09bd939cf895","4ee17362488e426ab128ca30680dc8c0","ddfce8b9379f44ababf56fdb9542a4d3","bebbdcfa918148bdb11ee393cba232b2","eedcb93d3cdf48e4bdcf71ec22e2406a","110335479dfe4d389d160ffc8a717d4b","40f56e331f5241ad8b18662e7dd53051","140f3d0395994c34bb62512d19d9e086","083f5c2ad5444ec99b4a9788b4b7adf1","40994ecc3a7443b9b50644908aefe765","9473336653b34d819eea74bcf72a8db5","6f4d55bef294479c8bdd7c9cbd5bfb54","837581db9ca14a3182ed95c8da660e28","c94980f1b23c4304b7b10c8fd7d965cf","d4cafd0f49594ef081dbd7e2b427a441","c431cede1aa3420280ebc1b66723649f","db8054054d394b2099347304c7b6b832","8c0aeb3b485e4944a0acfbc50796474f","7b4af4d202334117821a442f4356e12f","a6216c46f3bd44f38160b65bcbaf71fd","e0b52d69e0684da5a33925972a26095f","5a8fae9aac7b4d41be5f9b8ad3ef9920","af5dd82b62454070a25f415bbf31a13a","16eaf9590a1e4eacabf7e0490d6250f8","0b64850fc08a47eea73929d642086167","e58f0abe08aa460393d1d1f6419979c8","1411c817e5a34d2ab0c044e317dba5d7","dbd5c32273fa4ce882eeb4d3772f9f63","e77ed82e69c74abba986b215104d76de","d5ccfcf3c5d04b19825d8da606a8f5a0","6a0b8d6a923e4863aa7b173683d8d147","6f2192dc6831475aaceaf018828578b6","c63467d9626340308b4f2428b5be537a","d8ee9f716fa848a79c1b65bdac94070d","4625381553e44b4f85adc6c88cc87b6a","a0bb7db2c67f459cbd668e19879feb06","32b5449323d843e29e9fd6eeebc79526","18f286ecdd8a4d418bfd5ae8d14c9c00","937e84686f7249049b8451f9f715bc6b","acb9a56307a84aa2b5d8e540d2ff6939","f48767c2b0c74906bc836fbb91bff51b","b0c15f4dc0ad4560a36a6d5009b75580","35bd146c41ae4a11be730852a411d840","226252a458494f4eb12dd1aa8f35ea68","f0ea3df8fb664420a42ef5a82e241ef1","3a3d3a03ad8a4f6e9b754afb4a4611ff