 done using popular deep learning frameworks such as PyTorch or TensorFlow.\n","\n","<li>Replace the final fully connected layer: The final layer of the pre-trained ResNet34 model is a fully connected layer with 1000 output neurons corresponding to the number of classes in ImageNet. This layer needs to be replaced with a new fully connected layer with the number of output neurons equal to the number of classes in the new dataset.\n","\n","<li>Freeze the pre-trained layers: The weights of the pre-trained layers are frozen so that only the weights of the new fully connected layer are updated during training. This ensures that the learned features from the pre-trained model are preserved and only the classification layer is adapted to the new task.\n","\n","<li>Prepare the new dataset: The new dataset needs to be prepared by splitting it into training, validation, and test sets and resizing the images to the required input size of the pre-trained ResNet34 model.\n","\n","<li>Train the model: The model is trained on the new dataset with a small learning rate, allowing the weights of the new fully connected layer to be updated gradually while preserving the learned features of the pre-trained layers.\n","\n","<li>Evaluate the model: The performance of the fine-tuned ResNet34 model is evaluated on the test set to measure its accuracy and other performance metrics.\n","\n","<p style=\"font-family:Georgia;\">ResNet34 transfer learning is a potent method that, while using the learnt features from the pre-trained model, may considerably cut the amount of training data and the amount of time needed to construct a high-performing model for a new job. It has been demonstrated to work well for a number of computer vision applications, including segmentation, object identification, and picture classification."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"1K5-IUMWpRAa"},"outputs":[],"source":["resnet34pre_train = models.resnet34(pretrained=True)\n","num_classes = 