ed ResNet50 model, which can be easily done using popular deep learning frameworks such as PyTorch or TensorFlow.\n","\n","<li>Replace the final fully connected layer: The final layer of the pre-trained ResNet50 model is a fully connected layer with 1000 output neurons corresponding to the number of classes in ImageNet. This layer needs to be replaced with a new fully connected layer with the number of output neurons equal to the number of classes in the new dataset.\n","\n","<li>Freeze the pre-trained layers: The weights of the pre-trained layers are frozen so that only the weights of the new fully connected layer are updated during training. This ensures that the learned features from the pre-trained model are preserved and only the classification layer is adapted to the new task.\n","\n","<li>Prepare the new dataset: The new dataset needs to be prepared by splitting it into training, validation, and test sets and resizing the images to the required input size of the pre-trained ResNet50 model.\n","\n","<li>Train the model: The model is trained on the new dataset with a small learning rate, allowing the weights of the new fully connected layer to be updated gradually while preserving the learned features of the pre-trained layers.\n","\n","<li>Evaluate the model: The performance of the fine-tuned ResNet50 model is evaluated on the test set to measure its accuracy and other performance metrics.\n","    \n","<p style=\"font-family:Georgia;\">ResNet50 transfer learning is a powerful technique that can significantly reduce the amount of training data and time required to develop a high-performing model for a new task, while leveraging the learned features from the pre-trained model. It has been shown to be effective in a variety of computer vision tasks, including image classification, object detection, and segmentation."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"GlUcQQId_sfj","outputId":"db2da871-711