ayers: The weights of the pre-trained layers are frozen so that only the weights of the new fully connected layer are updated during training. This ensures that the learned features from the pre-trained model are preserved and only the classification layer is adapted to the new task.\n","\n","<li>Prepare the new dataset: The new dataset needs to be prepared by splitting it into training, validation, and test sets and resizing the images to the required input size of the pre-trained MobileNet model.\n","\n","<li>Train the model: The model is trained on the new dataset with a small learning rate, allowing the weights of the new fully connected layer to be updated gradually while preserving the learned features of the pre-trained layers.\n","\n","<li>Evaluate the model: The performance of the fine-tuned MobileNet model is evaluated on the test set to measure its accuracy and other performance metrics.\n","\n","<p style=\"font-family:Georgia;\">MobileNet transfer learning is a powerful technique that can significantly reduce the amount of training data and time required to develop a high-performing model for a new task, while leveraging the learned features from the pre-trained model. MobileNet is a popular choice for transfer learning in computer vision tasks because it is designed to be lightweight and efficient, making it suitable for deployment on mobile and embedded devices."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"YyDZo6Ad1d6v"},"outputs":[],"source":["mobilenet_v2_pre_train = models.mobilenet_v2(pretrained=True)\n","num_classes = 15\n","mobilenet_v2_pre_train.fc = nn.Linear(1280, num_classes)"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"_QSKIzlA8ERz"},"outputs":[],"source":["freeze_to(mobilenet_v2_pre_train, -1, True)"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":581,"referenced_widgets":["021aaa0e00744c9abcb632b22614222b","4f25de9761624a1f86bdb7516047e767